<title>VENEZUELA: ANDES BANK LOANS VENEZUELA $110MLN FOR POWER LINES.</title>
<headline>ANDES BANK LOANS VENEZUELA $110MLN FOR POWER LINES.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Regional development bank, the Andean Development Corporation (CAF), said Wednesday it had loaned Venezuela $110 million to build three power lines in the south and southeast of the country.</p>
<p>The lines, to be constructed and managed by state electricity company EDELCA, would provide power to mining and oil companies in the region, the CAF said in a release.</p>
<p>One of the lines would supply the Las Cristinas gold mining development in Bolivar state currently disputed by Canada's Placer Dome and Crystallex.</p>
<p>The CAF is the financial arm of the five-nation Andean Community trade bloc of Venezuela, Colombia, Bolivia, Ecuador and Peru.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
